<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>

<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name      "claude-ssh">
  <!ENTITY author    "Patrick">
  <!ENTITY version   "2026.05.13g">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "https://github.com/ctrlbreak/unraid-claude-ssh-plugin/releases/latest/download/&name;.plg">
  <!ENTITY pkgURL    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;.txz">
  <!ENTITY pkgRemote "https://github.com/ctrlbreak/unraid-claude-ssh-plugin/releases/download/v&version;/&name;.txz">
  <!ENTITY md5       "__MD5__">
  <!ENTITY cfgDir    "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
  <!ENTITY emhttpDir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" icon="key">

<CHANGES>
###2026.05.13g
- **Simplify the Plugins-page icon.** The PNG-shipping approach from
  `2026.05.13d/e` is gone. The `.plg` now declares `icon="key"` as a
  `&lt;PLUGIN&gt;` attribute, which Unraid resolves to the FontAwesome
  `fa-key` glyph — same library and same glyph the Dashboard tile
  and Settings tab already render via `Icon="key"` in their `.page`
  headers. `dynamix.plugin.manager/include/ShowPlugins.php`'s
  `plugin('icon',$plugin_file)` path treats non-`.png` icon values as
  FA class names directly.
- Drops the PNG (`claude-ssh.png`), the FontAwesome CC BY 4.0
  attribution from README, and the build-time assertion that the
  PNG is packaged. Three earlier releases of qlmanage/alpha-channel
  fiddling collapse into one `.plg` attribute.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged from
  `2026.05.13b/c/d/e/f` (filter v11, writer v6).

###2026.05.13f
- **Restore plugin name on the Plugins page.** The README shipped in
  `2026.05.13e` was a single paragraph; Unraid's `ShowPlugins.php`
  uses it verbatim and drops the `**&lt;name&gt;**` fallback when a README
  exists. Result: every other plugin on the page showed
  bold-name-then-description, but `claude-ssh` showed just the
  description. Fix: prepend `**Claude SSH**` as its own line so the
  rendered Markdown carries both the title and the blurb.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged from
  `2026.05.13b/c/d/e` (filter v11, writer v6).

###2026.05.13e
- **Plugin icon: black on transparent.** The icon shipped in `2026.05.13d`
  rendered onto an opaque white canvas (qlmanage thumbnailer behaviour),
  producing a green key inside a visible white box on the Plugins page —
  out of step with the Dashboard tile, which renders FontAwesome
  `fa-key` in the page's text colour. This release re-renders the same
  FontAwesome `fa-key` glyph in pure black and post-processes the PNG
  alpha so the background is genuinely transparent. The Plugins page
  now shows a black key flush against the row background, matching the
  Settings tab and Dashboard tile.
- **Plugins-page description.** Ships a short `README.md` at
  `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-ssh/README.md` so the Unraid plugin
  manager renders a description line under the plugin name (matching
  how Community Applications and Dynamix plugins show their summaries).
  Unraid's `ShowPlugins.php` reads this file as Markdown; without it,
  the page falls back to just the bold plugin name.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged from
  `2026.05.13b/c/d` (filter v11, writer v6).

###2026.05.13d
- **Plugin icon on the Plugins page.** Ships a 128x128 PNG at
  `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-ssh/claude-ssh.png` so the Unraid
  plugin manager shows a key icon instead of the default green puzzle.
  Visually matches the FontAwesome `fa-key` icon the Settings tab and
  Dashboard tile already use. Derived from FontAwesome Free 5's
  `fa-key` glyph (CC BY 4.0); attribution in README's License section.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged from
  `2026.05.13b/c` (filter v11, writer v6).

###2026.05.13c
- **MIT LICENSE shipped in the package.** The repo gained an MIT LICENSE
  file at the previous release boundary; this release also stages it
  into the plugin tree at build time so installed copies carry the
  license at `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-ssh/LICENSE`.
  `tests/test-build.sh` now asserts the file is in the `.txz`.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged from
  `2026.05.13b` (filter v11, writer v6).

###2026.05.13b
- **Collapse `plugin-{page,include,script,cfg}` into a single `plugin-file`
  category.** New argv shape: `claude-write plugin-file &lt;plugin&gt; &lt;rel-path&gt;`,
  where `&lt;rel-path&gt;` is a relative path under
  `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&lt;plugin&gt;/` with up to 3 components. Filter `v10
  → v11`, writer `v5 → v6`.
- **Extension allowlist** (set on the writer):
  `.page .php .cfg .sh .py .js .css .html .svg .txt .json`. Mode is driven by
  extension — `.sh` / `.py` → 755, everything else → 644.
- **Extensionless `event/&lt;hook&gt;` exception** (Unraid event-hook convention):
  basename must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,32}$`, depth-1 only, mode 755. No
  other extensionless writes are permitted.
- **Sudoers** enumerates three rel-path arities (`plugin-file * *`,
  `plugin-file * */*`, `plugin-file * */*/*`) because sudo's `*` wildcard
  does not match `/`. Old `plugin-{page,include,script,cfg}` grants removed.
- **BREAKING for direct claude-write callers.** Scripts using the old
  category names need updating to `plugin-file &lt;plugin&gt; &lt;rel-path&gt;`.
  No transitional alias.
- exec.php counters: dropped the four `plugin-*` rows; added `plugin-file`.
- Settings UI label updated; stale `/boot/config/...` reference on the
  Allowlist heading swapped for the real `/mnt/user/appdata/...` path.

###2026.05.13a
- **Dashboard tile redesign.** Adopts the Unraid 7.x `$mytiles[column1]` API
  so the tile now sits inside the dashboard's column grid (half-width like
  every other tile) instead of rendering as a full-width banner above the
  columns. Gated on Unraid 6.12+ via the `Cond=` page header; older versions
  silently skip the tile.
- **Richer tile content.** Shows installation health (user, filter, writer,
  sudoers, SSH-key count) as inline tick/cross badges, 24h activity broken
  out into accepted / blocked / writes / rejected, and the allowlist size
  (plugins + containers). Status verdict pill (Healthy / activity blocked /
  Not installed) sits in the tile-header subtitle.
- **Backend** `dashboard` action returns one richer JSON blob per 60s poll —
  same single AJAX call, no extra backend load. Allowlist counts derive from
  the same `load_allowlist_file()` the Settings UI uses, so the tile and
  editor can never disagree.
- **New** `tests/test-dashboard-action.sh` pins the JSON shape (19 cases).
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged.

###2026.05.12e
- **Simplified install banners.** The SSH-setup script's "Setup complete!"
  block dropped from ~30 lines to ~10 (14 lines of filter-rule detail moved
  to docs/filter.md, test examples trimmed from 6 to 2). The claude-write
  banner dropped from ~42 lines to ~10 (16 lines of category detail moved
  to docs/categories.md, dual workstation-usage examples merged into one).
- **Dropped the obsolete "NEXT: redeploy unraid-readonly-ssh-setup.sh" line**
  from the writer banner. It was a leftover from the standalone-install
  workflow; under the plugin, install-runtime.sh calls both setup scripts
  in sequence, so the filter is already redeployed by the time the user
  reads the writer banner.
- **install-runtime.sh now prints a closing summary** with three concrete
  next steps (add SSH key, edit allowlist, check Settings tab) and a
  pointer to verify-install.sh for deeper end-to-end verification.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged.

###2026.05.12d
- **Centralise filter/writer version literals.** Each setup script now
  declares its runtime-contract version as a single shell variable at the
  top (`FILTER_VERSION` / `WRITER_VERSION`); install banners and exec.php's
  Status-page parser both read that one assignment. Removes the bug class
  where a hardcoded `vN` in an install banner stayed stale after a bump.
- **New `tests/test-version-drift.sh`.** Scans user-facing docs for
  current-tense filter/writer version claims (badges, diagram annotations,
  sample output) and fails CI if any disagrees with canonical. Historical
  release notes (CHANGELOG.md, the .plg CHANGES block) are not scanned.
- **Drift-affected docs cleaned up.** Generic phrasings now point at
  `FILTER_VERSION` / `WRITER_VERSION` rather than naming a specific
  current value (`install.md`, `threat-model.md`, `verifying.md`,
  `troubleshooting.md`, `wire-protocol.md`, `categories.md`). README's
  "Versions" section was already replaced with a "Versioning" rationale.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged.

###2026.05.12c
- **Move allowlist off `/boot/config`.** Filter `v9 → v10`, writer `v4 → v5`.
  The constrained SSH user could never read the allowlist when it lived in
  `/boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/` because `/boot` is FAT-mounted with
  `dmask=0077` (kernel-forces every dir there to mode 700 regardless of
  chmod). New canonical location: `/mnt/user/appdata/claude-ssh/allowlist.cfg`,
  on the array with normal Unix perms (mode 644).
- **One-shot migration on upgrade.** `install-runtime.sh` copies any
  existing `/boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/allowlist.cfg` to the new
  location and renames the legacy file to `*.migrated-pre-v2026.05.12c`
  so it's clearly out of service. Settings UI saves go to the new path
  atomically.
- **Username file stays put** at `/boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/username`.
  Only read by root (install-runtime.sh, claude-write-setup.sh, exec.php) —
  the FAT mask doesn't affect that path's usability.
- Banner version labels in setup scripts caught up (`v7 → v10`, `v2 → v5`).

###2026.05.12b
- **Fix allowlist unreadable by constrained user.** install-runtime.sh now
  explicitly `chmod 755 /boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/` (idempotent —
  fixes existing installs where the dir was created with mode 700 from
  earlier root umask). Without world-execute on the dir, the SSH filter
  silently default-denies every `claude-write plugin-*` and
  `claude-write appdata-script` invocation because it can't stat
  `allowlist.cfg`. Surfaced during first live deploy: every Layer-3 write
  in `verify-install.sh` was rejected as "not in allowlist" despite the
  entries being present.
- No filter/writer version bump — runtime artifacts unchanged.

###2026.05.12a
- **Fix .plg FILE block ordering.** The `&pkgURL;` download block now
  precedes the install script, so `upgradepkg` runs against the freshly-
  downloaded `.txz` instead of whatever was cached on flash. Previously
  the install script ran first and used a stale (or missing) cached
  `.txz`, causing silent regressions on upgrades and outright install
  failures for fresh adopters.
- **Filter version banner fixed.** `unraid-readonly-ssh-setup.sh`'s
  install-time output line said "Filter: ... v7" — a stale label not
  bumped when filter went v7 → v8 → v9. Now reads v9. Runtime artifact
  unchanged (the deployed filter has always carried the correct
  `# Filter version:` marker; this was install-stdout cosmetic only).
- No runtime behaviour changes from `2026.05.07a` — filter `v9`, writer
  `v4` unchanged.

###2026.05.07a
- First public release. Repo published at
  https://github.com/ctrlbreak/unraid-claude-ssh-plugin and the plugin is
  installable from the Unraid web UI by pasting the release .plg URL:
  https://github.com/ctrlbreak/unraid-claude-ssh-plugin/releases/latest/download/claude-ssh.plg
- .plg now points at the GitHub release for the matching version (rather
  than expecting a side-loaded .txz on flash) and declares an MD5 hash so
  the plugin manager verifies integrity before extracting.
- The Unraid plugin update check now resolves against
  releases/latest/download/claude-ssh.plg, so installed instances detect new
  releases automatically.
- No runtime behaviour changes from 2026.05.06c — filter v9 and writer v4
  unchanged. This release is the publishing event, not a feature.

###2026.05.06c
- Configurable SSH username (setup-time only). Setup scripts read
  CLAUDE_SSH_USERNAME from env or /boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/username
  (single-line file), defaulting to "claude". Validated against
  ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$. Existing installs unaffected — defaults match
  prior behaviour.
- install-runtime.sh resolves the username, exports it for child setup
  scripts, and seeds the persisted file on first install (never overwritten,
  so explicit user choice survives).
- claude-write-setup.sh substitutes the resolved username into the sudoers
  principal so a non-default SSH user receives the matching grants.
- exec.php derives /home/&lt;user&gt;/ paths and the /etc/passwd existence
  check from the same source. Status payload exposes the configured
  username so the Settings page surfaces it on the Health KPI.
- New test-username-configurable.sh: drift check across the four shell
  scripts, env/file/default precedence, validation rejects, sudoers
  principal parameterisation, install-runtime seeding (32 cases).

###2026.05.06b
- Settings UI: Allowlist editor on the Settings/Status tab. Two textareas for
  plugin and container names, Save and Reload buttons, status pane.
  Server-side validation against the same name regex used by the filter and
  writer. Atomic write to allowlist.cfg via temp-file plus rename. Header
  comment block is regenerated on every save (manual edits to comments and
  unrelated lines are not preserved through the UI).
- exec.php: new load_allowlist and save_allowlist routes; helper functions
  load_allowlist_file and save_allowlist_file are also callable directly
  from PHP CLI for tests (dispatcher early-returns under cli SAPI).
- Tests: new test-settings-save.sh exercises the save/load round-trip with
  a 35-case sandbox suite (skips if php is not installed).
  test-claude-write-validation.sh extended to assert exec.php uses the same
  allowlist path default, env-var override, and name regex as the shell side.

###2026.05.06a
- Filter v9 + writer v4: hook-sonarr/hook-radarr categories collapsed into
  a generic appdata-script category. New 3-arg form: container name plus
  basename, target /mnt/user/appdata/CONTAINER/scripts/. Container
  allowlist added to allowlist.cfg as "container NAME" lines (same parser
  and name regex as the plugin allowlist; default-deny when empty).
  Allowlist parser is now parametric on line-prefix; filter and writer
  both reuse it.
- BREAKING: hook-sonarr / hook-radarr no longer accepted. Migrate to
  "appdata-script sonarr" / "appdata-script radarr" and add the matching
  "container" lines to allowlist.cfg.
- exec.php counters: dropped hook-sonarr/hook-radarr rows; added appdata-script.
- install-runtime.sh seed template extended with container examples.

###2026.05.06
- Filter v8 + writer v3: plugin-name allowlist moved to runtime config at
  /boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/allowlist.cfg. Default-deny when empty.
- install-runtime.sh seeds a commented-template allowlist.cfg on first install
  (existing files never overwritten).
- New tests: test-allowlist-config.sh (parser behaviour) +
  test-boot-config-write-block.sh (filter blocks writes to /boot/config/).

###2026.05.04
- Initial release: packages claude SSH filter v7 + claude-write writer v2
- Single-tab Status page with collapsible Audit Log section
- Dashboard tile showing filter version + 24h activity
- Filter v7: plugin-name parameterised plugin-* categories, new scratch category
- Idempotent install/upgrade — re-runs setup scripts, single /boot/config/go entry
- Non-destructive uninstall — preserves /home/claude/, backups, user account
</CHANGES>

<!--
Package file. Downloaded from the GitHub release matching this .plg's
version entity. CI substitutes the real md5 into &md5; on tag push; the
in-repo .plg has __MD5__ as a placeholder and is not directly installable
— always install from a release URL (see docs/install.md).

MUST come before the install script below: Unraid processes FILE blocks
in document order, so the .txz needs to land on flash before
upgradepkg runs.
-->
<FILE Name="&pkgURL;">
<URL>&pkgRemote;</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<!--
Install / upgrade script. The .txz (downloaded by the FILE block above)
extracts the plugin tree to /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/claude-ssh/, then
install-runtime.sh runs the filter + writer setup scripts and registers
the boot hook.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash

PLUGIN="claude-ssh"
CFG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/${PLUGIN}"

echo "Installing ${PLUGIN}..."

# Create config directory on flash (preserves user state across upgrades)
mkdir -p "${CFG_DIR}"

# Install or upgrade the package. --reinstall ensures all files in the .txz
# overwrite the previous version cleanly (without it, identical paths from
# older versions can stick around).
upgradepkg --install-new --reinstall "&pkgURL;"

# Run the runtime installer: deploys the SSH filter + claude-write writer
# and registers the boot hook in /boot/config/go.
bash "&emhttpDir;/scripts/install-runtime.sh"

echo "${PLUGIN} installed."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
Remove script. Non-destructive: tears down runtime artifacts (sudoers, sshd
config additions, claude-write binaries, /boot/config/go hook) but leaves
/home/claude/, the claude user, and the backup directory intact.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash

PLUGIN="claude-ssh"
echo "Removing ${PLUGIN}..."

# Run uninstall-runtime.sh BEFORE removepkg — needs the script to exist.
if [ -x "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/${PLUGIN}/scripts/uninstall-runtime.sh" ]; then
    bash "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/${PLUGIN}/scripts/uninstall-runtime.sh"
fi

# Remove the package. Config dir on flash is preserved.
removepkg "${PLUGIN}"

echo "${PLUGIN} removed. Config preserved at /boot/config/plugins/${PLUGIN}/"
echo "To fully purge: userdel claude &amp;&amp; rm -rf /home/claude /mnt/cache/appdata/claude-write-backups"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
